_2":{"wt":"40,920"},"city_3":{"wt":"Kyrenia"},"div_3":{"wt":"Girne District{{!}}Girne"},"pop_3":{"wt":"33,207"},"city_4":{"wt":"Morphou"},"div_4":{"wt":"Güzelyurt District{{!}}Güzelyurt"},"pop_4":{"wt":"18,946"},"city_5":{"wt":"Gönyeli"},"div_5":{"wt":"Lefkoşa District{{!}}Lefkoşa"},"pop_5":{"wt":"17,277"},"city_6":{"wt":"Kythrea"},"div_6":{"wt":"Lefkoşa District{{!}}Lefkoşa"},"pop_6":{"wt":"11,895"},"city_7":{"wt":"Lefka"},"div_7":{"wt":"Lefke District{{!}}Lefke"},"pop_7":{"wt":"11,091"},"city_8":{"wt":"Dikomo"},"div_8":{"wt":"Girne District{{!}}Girne"},"pop_8":{"wt":"9,120"},"city_9":{"wt":"Trikomo, Cyprus{{!}}Trikomo"},"div_9":{"wt":"İskele District{{!}}İskele"},"pop_9":{"wt":"7,906"},"city_10":{"wt":"Lapithos"},"div_10":{"wt":"Girne District{{!}}Girne"},"pop_10":{"wt":"7,839"}},"i":1}}]}' id="mwBLQ">There are 644 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Greek_Cypriot" title="Greek Cypriot" class="mw-redirect">Greek Cypriots</a> living in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Rizokarpaso" title="Rizokarpaso">Rizokarpaso</a> (Dipkarpaz) and 364 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Maronites" title="Maronites">Maronites</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Kormakitis" title="Kormakitis">Kormakitis</a>.<sup about="#mwt548" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-153" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-153"}}'><a href="./Northern_Cyprus#cite_note-153" id="mwBLU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLc">[</span>151<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLg">]</span></span></a></sup> 162,000<sup about="#mwt551" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-154" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-154"}}'><a href="./Northern_Cyprus#cite_note-154" id="mwBLk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLs">[</span>152<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLw">]</span></span></a></sup> Greek Cypriots were forcibly evicted from their homes in the North by the invading force of the Turkish army.<sup about="#mwt554" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Denver_journal_of_international_law_and_policy_155-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Denver journal of international law and policy"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Denver_journal_of_international_law_and_policy-155"}}'><a href="./Northern_Cyprus#cite_note-Denver_journal_of_international_law_and_policy-155" id="mwBL0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBL4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBL8">[</span>153<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt557" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Mallinson2011_156-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Mallinson2011"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Mallinson2011-156"}}'><a href="./Northern_Cyprus#cite_note-Mallinson2011-156" id="mwBME"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBMI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMM">[</span>154<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt560" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HörnerDöbert2006_157-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HörnerDöbert2006"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HörnerDöbert2006-157"}}'><a href="./Northern_Cyprus#cite_note-HörnerDöbert2006-157" id="mwBMU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBMY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMc">[</span>155<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMg">]</span></span></a></sup> Rizokarpaso is the home of the biggest Greek-speaking population in the north. The Greek-Cypriot inhabitants are still supplied by the UN, and Greek-Cypriot products are consequently available in some shops.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category